   "since": "2026-09-01",
   "unit": null,
   "value": "The Regulatory Information Service Center (the Center) compiles the Unified Agenda for the Office of Information and Regulatory Affairs (OIRA), part of the Office of Management and Budget. OIRA is responsible for overseeing the Federal Government's regulatory, paperwork, and information resource management activities, including implementation of Executive Order 12866, as amended. The Center also provides information about Federal regulatory activity to the President and his Executive Office, the Congress, agency managers, and the public.",
